/-!
# H3.4 (centre generator on the canonical chart): `pivotTorsion w = powerSat ⊥ (ψ g)`

Lane G10H3, run 0081 (field `T_w₀` of `HironakaG10NfGeoFibreModel.GeoFibreModel`; also the `g`-field of G10GL's pulled
presentations).  Canonical setting of `HironakaG10SbCanonicalStrictTorsion`.  At every source chart point `w` of the
fibre-product locus (`hV : actualMap w ∈ targetStrict`, `w` NOT assumed on the strict transform), with
`ψ := targetStalkToJoint ∘ (targetChartMap j)^♯` (G10GL's `canonicalPsi`) and every regular generator `G` of the pulled
centre at `Q := targetChartMap ⟨actualMap w, hV⟩`:

* `chart_span_eq` — on the target strict chart the pulled centre is generated by the pivot coordinate class
  (`TargetExplicitNormalLaws.whole_ideal` + `strict_pivot_generator_locus`);
* `psi_pivot` — `ψ` sends that class to the pivot class (`targetStalkToJoint_pivot`, `lift_pivot_flatCoord`);
* **`pivotTorsion_eq_powerSat_canonical`** — `pivotTorsion w = powerSat ⊥ (ψ G)`.

No named input.
-/

